Article 9 (Operations Headquarters)
(1) The Operations Headquarters shall have one director, who shall be a general officer. <Amended on September 5, 2017>
(2) The director shall be responsible for:
1. Planning, direction, and control of military operations;
2. Crisis management and maintenance of wartime transition systems;
3. Determination and request of operational planning requirements and readiness assessment;
4. Integrated civilian-government-military defense operations and training;
4-2. Psychological warfare, information operations, and cyber operations;
5. Engineer operations;
6. Operational review concerning protection of military facilities;
7. Submission of reserve force requirements;
8. Formulation and support of policies on joint, combined, and unit training;
9. Operation of the Joint Chiefs of Staff command and control room. <Amended on December 27, 2012; February 16, 2015; December 30, 2022>
